{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/819403-spirit-allies","id":819403,"title":"Spirit allies","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-29T11:57:34-08:00","id":819403,"title":"Spirit allies","content":"Is there someway some way for my Theurge to get a couple of sprits to follow me around and help protect me? To keep an eye out for me in the penumbra?<br /> <br /> Im assuming that some chiminage is appropriate, but what?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/ghw20supporterhiddengaroup\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/n18segp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0v25ewp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">English is not my native language, so i apologize for errors in grammar or spelling.</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/392-cadmiumcadamium","name":"Cadmiumcadamium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar392_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"936"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T13:58:07-08:00","id":819490,"title":"","content":"I would be hesitant to allow such a feat, for it would surpass the power of even mid-level gifts and I don't really find that appropriate.<br /> <br /> Besides that, there are some logical gaps. <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Spirits in the Penumbra following the character would still have to deal with all penumbral affairs, like spirits living there, differences between the landscape/umbrascape and such. Also, if the character would move fast, like with a car or train, they would probably not be able to follow under their own power. Being able to find the character again, would require them to have 'Tracking' charm.</li> <li>To warn the character while not in the penumbra, they would need 'Appear', Materialize or some form of a telepathy charm. That is unless the Theurge has the appropriate level three gift, that allows him to see spirits in the umbra whenever his Gnosis exceeds the Gauntlet.</li> </ol><br /> <br /> There are gifts and rites, like &quot;Urban ward&quot; to have warning capabilities. And obviously, you could bind a spirit into an item and release it Pokeball-style to fight for you. Such a binding would be semi-permanent as in a duration of a lunar months per success in the rite.<br /> <br /> Given that totems require devotion and a certain degree of worship and adherence to their way of life and they basically offer, that you become their ward in some way and they look out for you to some degree, I'd guess that this is the benchmark for chiminage.<br /> <br /> That said, if you can't find a spirit that can <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Perceive penumbra and material world simultaniously</li> <li>Is able to communicate with you, even when you are on the other side of the Gauntlet.</li> <li>Is able to keep up with you, even if you travel with technological means.</li> <li>Is able to move around in the penumbra without being bothered by wandering spirits or spirits through who's territory it might have to move to follow you.</li> </ol><br /> then you probably better settle on a spirit that you can form a relation ship with, or that has a guardian aspect. In this case, you might find a spirit that has a charm &quot;Domain sense&quot; with domain being it's ward, meaning your character. In this case, the spirit could possibly clairvoyant any dangers you might experience. Such a spirit bound into a fetish might even be a substitute for the &quot;Danger Sense&quot; merit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-30T17:43:48-08:00","id":820050,"title":"","content":"You need to treat spirits the same way as people - they all have their own motivations, desires, and goals. Following you around and protecting you all the time isn't one of them. Even friends who will help you out when needed aren't going to spend their free time, much less their life, doing that.<br /> <br /> Of course, in real life the rich can hire bodyguards, which is what this would be. But the rich are paying multiple people high salaries to do so. What is the equivalent chiminage for that? It's probably a lot more Gnosis and favors then you can pay.<br /> <br /> Here I think are more realistic options.<br /> <br /> Paying chiminage for specific tasks that can be completed, or for short established time frames. So it is not an all the time kind of thing. It's during when you think you need it most.<br /> <br /> Or find a powerful Jaggling who has control of all sorts of gafflings, and can sell out to him. Then the jaggling will send various gaffling minions out to watch over you. But at that point, you are heavily in debt. You owe the jaggling long term favors (because you need to keep paying for all the favors he's doing you). That'll include a lot of Gnosis, ongoing behavior that you'll incorporate into your downtime and routines, and giving the ST a means to drive lots of plot through you.<br /> <br /> The best way to is create an appropriate Fetish out of those one or two spirits instead. One fetish that provides some kind of &quot;warning&quot; - lower difficulty for Perception to avoid surprise, or extra die to those rolls, and a second fetish with similar properties to help you in the Penumbra - say to do Sense Wyrm there while you are still in the Realm. This will probably work better for you long term.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T00:17:19-08:00","id":820199,"title":"","content":"In addition to what Black Fox and Heinrich said, I would also say the spirits are not particularly inclined to intervene in combat since Garou are the warriors of Gaia. Many spirits will help the Garou indirectly and otherwise, but to a certain extent werewolves are expected to bear the brunt of the fighting (sort of why cops and soldiers don't have bodyguards- they take the fight to the enemy themselves). After all, why should the fangs and claws of the Mother require protection?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T23:48:52-08:00","id":820784,"title":"","content":"The combat option of the Philodox gift &quot;Call of Duty&quot; not withstanding....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T01:14:02-08:00","id":820825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/819403-spirit-allies?p=820199#post820199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In addition to what Black Fox and Heinrich said, I would also say the spirits are not particularly inclined to intervene in combat since Garou are the warriors of Gaia. Many spirits will help the Garou indirectly and otherwise, but to a certain extent werewolves are expected to bear the brunt of the fighting (sort of why cops and soldiers don't have bodyguards- they take the fight to the enemy themselves). After all, why should the fangs and claws of the Mother require protection?</div> </div> </div> </div>Still, I could see it a a possible thing for an individual Spirit. There are Spirits of War and beating the crap out of stuff, I'm pretty sure they are pretty damn beligerent and you could get them to fight for you. There is also the option that a spirit might be indebted to a character or his bloodline (an Ally) and who might look out for an individual Garou.<br /> <br /> I still don't see it as either of those Spirits being capable of constantly being around and watching out for him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}